[node name="S3_Minefield" type="Node3D" parent="Sections" unique_id=61707270]
editor_description = "S3, the demon pad grid (bearings 145..200). The deck is flat at lane height and tiled with these demon_pad nodes in rows along the arc and columns across the width; one path is carved through the grid by the cells left pad-free, three pads left in the path (trigger 0.5 m tall) have to be jumped, and the half wall along the path's pit side is map_base.glb's own rock. tools/modelling/map_base_build.py (the S3 block) is the one layout the mesh, the collider, these pad transforms and the proofs all come from; the build writes this node block. Every pad launches at the shipped 18 m/s; the 204 divider catches the flights that would leave the section. No lava and no TrapVolume in this section: a launch drops you back on the same deck. SpeedPowerup is a parked leftover from the retired Split, left where it was found."

